{"type": "message", "id": "9223cc33", "parentId": "9df1fbc3", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T22:34:05.818Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "chatcmpl-tool-8eeeb0439f692c0b", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:gold.ac.uk/pg \\\"Media, Communications and Cultural Studies\\\" MA programs list\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 968,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c0d5bcea810842ad\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMA Media & Communications | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c0d5bcea810842ad\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-media-communications/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32f83c242e0d7bb0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFounded in 1993, this Master&#x27;s programme reflects the research-led interdisciplinary approach we take to media and communications that has made us leaders in the field. We value the creative and the critical and their interrelationships, to explore and interrogate how the complex, mediated worlds we live in work. You’ll study in one of the top Media, Communications and Cultural Studies schools globally.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"32f83c242e0d7bb0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f5baf86c9d7caa2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMA Cultural Studies | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f5baf86c9d7caa2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-cultural-studies/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d8e0ebbbd80f38bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThese span the fields of <strong>music, film, digital media, aesthetics, cultural industries, gender and queer studies, postcolonialism, journalism, political economy, critical race studies, and critical theory</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d8e0ebbbd80f38bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"130b751d00dee406\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMPhil/PhD Media, Communications and Cultural Studies | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"130b751d00dee406\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/mphil-phd-media-communications-cultural-studies/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3bebfb42eb55bab9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMembers of the Department edit leading academic journals, including Body and Society, Culture Machine and its sister project, Photomediations Machine), Global Media and Communication, International Journal of Cultural Studies, Subjectivity and photographies. The Department’s research falls into five main strands which make up our research groupings: Building on the work of the Leverhulme programme on the media’s contribution to democracy, including the changing nature of journalism and political communication; studying globalisation in relation to issues of diaspora and nationhood.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3bebfb42eb55bab9\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5d3c2c87640817f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMRes Media & Communications | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5d3c2c87640817f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/mres-media-communications/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd89f7081502e543\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMembers of the school edit leading academic journals, including Body and Society, Culture Machine and its sister project, Photomediations Machine), Global Media and Communication, International Journal of Cultural Studies, Subjectivity and photographies. ... Media and Democracy: building on the work of the Leverhulme programme on the media’s contribution to democracy, including the changing nature of journalism and political communication; studying globalisation in relation to issues of diaspora and nationhood\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd89f7081502e543\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5fc1351ef55fbcc1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMA Digital Media | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5fc1351ef55fbcc1\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-digital-media/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8042cdc83c1c6743\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn order to provide a contextual framework and facilitate the conceptualisation of digital media and technologies as fully cultural forms and processes, the programme will draw on a range of disciplines including: media and cultural studies, sociology, anthropology and philosophy.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8042cdc83c1c6743\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57fe193a9c401f16\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMedia, Communications and Cultural Studies modules | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"57fe193a9c401f16\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/media-modules/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1adbf1023a44852d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe School offers a wide range of option modules each year, which are taken in addition to the core modules on our Masters programmes. Below are some examples of those that have recently been offered by the School of Media, Communications and Cultural Studies.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1adbf1023a44852d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f14bb7682b30cb77\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMA Gender, Media & Culture | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f14bb7682b30cb77\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-gender-media-culture/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d21c225b6e747547\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis programme introduces you to recent debates on gender in the disciplines of sociology and media, as well as to the interdisciplinary domains of feminist social and cultural theory. There are a range of topic choices available, including embodiment, feminist methods, media and sexuality, and postcolonialism. You&#x27;ll be taught by experts in Sociology and Media, Communications and Cultural Studies, as well as the Centre for Feminist Research.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d21c225b6e747547\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3394fb200cf2aa76\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMA Brands, Communication & Culture | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3394fb200cf2aa76\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-brands-communication-culture/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93ba137e2084a605\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis is a trailblazing programme that gives you the skills, knowledge and experience to succeed at the highest levels in broadcast careers. The MA Cultural Studies offers an interdisciplinary approach to the study of contemporary to culture, politics and society. The MA Digital Media is unique in its combination of practical and theoretical approaches to contemporary media and technology.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93ba137e2084a605\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b9aea64cd911975\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMA Political Communications | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b9aea64cd911975\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-political-communications/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"affb6754435c74c0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe MA in Political Communications is built up of modules that must count up to 180 credits. The programme comprises: Two compulsory modules taught in the School of Media, Communications and Cultural Studies (60 credits in total)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"affb6754435c74c0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"857bbea889332ca4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMA Creative & Cultural Entrepreneurship | Goldsmiths, University of London\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"857bbea889332ca4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-creative-cultural-entrepreneurship-media/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a06fa58ba0ecd11\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGain an understanding of the cultural industries, with a focus on media and communications, on this MA degree at Goldsmiths, University of London.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2a06fa58ba0ecd11\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gold.ac.uk\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:gold.ac.uk/pg \"Media, Communications and Cultural Studies\" MA programs list", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 968, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c0d5bcea810842ad\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMA Media & Communications | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c0d5bcea810842ad\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-media-communications/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"32f83c242e0d7bb0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFounded in 1993, this Master&#x27;s programme reflects the research-led interdisciplinary approach we take to media and communications that has made us leaders in the field. We value the creative and the critical and their interrelationships, to explore and interrogate how the complex, mediated worlds we live in work. You’ll study in one of the top Media, Communications and Cultural Studies schools globally.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"32f83c242e0d7bb0\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2f5baf86c9d7caa2\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMA Cultural Studies | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2f5baf86c9d7caa2\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-cultural-studies/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d8e0ebbbd80f38bb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThese span the fields of <strong>music, film, digital media, aesthetics, cultural industries, gender and queer studies, postcolonialism, journalism, political economy, critical race studies, and critical theory</strong>.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d8e0ebbbd80f38bb\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"130b751d00dee406\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMPhil/PhD Media, Communications and Cultural Studies | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"130b751d00dee406\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/mphil-phd-media-communications-cultural-studies/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3bebfb42eb55bab9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMembers of the Department edit leading academic journals, including Body and Society, Culture Machine and its sister project, Photomediations Machine), Global Media and Communication, International Journal of Cultural Studies, Subjectivity and photographies. The Department’s research falls into five main strands which make up our research groupings: Building on the work of the Leverhulme programme on the media’s contribution to democracy, including the changing nature of journalism and political communication; studying globalisation in relation to issues of diaspora and nationhood.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3bebfb42eb55bab9\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5d3c2c87640817f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMRes Media & Communications | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5d3c2c87640817f\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/mres-media-communications/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd89f7081502e543\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMembers of the school edit leading academic journals, including Body and Society, Culture Machine and its sister project, Photomediations Machine), Global Media and Communication, International Journal of Cultural Studies, Subjectivity and photographies. ... Media and Democracy: building on the work of the Leverhulme programme on the media’s contribution to democracy, including the changing nature of journalism and political communication; studying globalisation in relation to issues of diaspora and nationhood\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd89f7081502e543\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5fc1351ef55fbcc1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMA Digital Media | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5fc1351ef55fbcc1\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-digital-media/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8042cdc83c1c6743\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn order to provide a contextual framework and facilitate the conceptualisation of digital media and technologies as fully cultural forms and processes, the programme will draw on a range of disciplines including: media and cultural studies, sociology, anthropology and philosophy.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8042cdc83c1c6743\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57fe193a9c401f16\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMedia, Communications and Cultural Studies modules | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"57fe193a9c401f16\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/media-modules/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1adbf1023a44852d\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe School offers a wide range of option modules each year, which are taken in addition to the core modules on our Masters programmes. Below are some examples of those that have recently been offered by the School of Media, Communications and Cultural Studies.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1adbf1023a44852d\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f14bb7682b30cb77\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMA Gender, Media & Culture | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"f14bb7682b30cb77\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-gender-media-culture/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d21c225b6e747547\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis programme introduces you to recent debates on gender in the disciplines of sociology and media, as well as to the interdisciplinary domains of feminist social and cultural theory. There are a range of topic choices available, including embodiment, feminist methods, media and sexuality, and postcolonialism. You&#x27;ll be taught by experts in Sociology and Media, Communications and Cultural Studies, as well as the Centre for Feminist Research.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d21c225b6e747547\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3394fb200cf2aa76\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMA Brands, Communication & Culture | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3394fb200cf2aa76\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-brands-communication-culture/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"93ba137e2084a605\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis is a trailblazing programme that gives you the skills, knowledge and experience to succeed at the highest levels in broadcast careers. The MA Cultural Studies offers an interdisciplinary approach to the study of contemporary to culture, politics and society. The MA Digital Media is unique in its combination of practical and theoretical approaches to contemporary media and technology.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"93ba137e2084a605\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b9aea64cd911975\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMA Political Communications | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b9aea64cd911975\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-political-communications/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"affb6754435c74c0\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe MA in Political Communications is built up of modules that must count up to 180 credits. The programme comprises: Two compulsory modules taught in the School of Media, Communications and Cultural Studies (60 credits in total)\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"affb6754435c74c0\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"857bbea889332ca4\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nMA Creative & Cultural Entrepreneurship | Goldsmiths, University of London\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"857bbea889332ca4\">>>", "url": "https://www.gold.ac.uk/pg/ma-creative-cultural-entrepreneurship-media/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2a06fa58ba0ecd11\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGain an understanding of the cultural industries, with a focus on media and communications, on this MA degree at Goldsmiths, University of London.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2a06fa58ba0ecd11\">>>", "siteName": "www.gold.ac.uk"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775774045817}}
